{
  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Kau. अत्यागेपि &c.—Even though the body is not cast off i. e.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "he will not have to wait for a second birth. संपत्स्यते—see",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Kum. II. 54 &c. स्पृहां संपत्स्यते v. l.—In this case संपद् must be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "understood as used transitively.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 92. कौपीनं—a small piece of cloth used to cover the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "privities. जर्जरतर—extremely ragged. चिन्ता act of contemplation.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Also a thought about (i. e. a wish for) a secluded place; ध्वस्ताशेष",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "&c.—delighted at the total destruction of egotism and errors;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "or मदात्प्रमादाः errors arising from egotism or pride.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 93. ब्रह्माण्डं मण्डलीमात्रं—v. l.—a mere circular body i. e.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "which is limited in space and not अपरिच्छिन्न like Brahman.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "This is perhaps a better reading. शफरी—a small fish. क्षुब्धता",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "जातु जायते—a question implying the negative answer in itself—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "'Is ever agitation produced &c.?'—'Never.' जातु ever, at",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "any time.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 94. मा स्म भूः–मा sometimes followed by स्म, is used with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "a form of the Imperf. or Aorist with the aug. अ dropped. Cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "क्लैब्यं मास्म गमः पार्थ &c. Bhg. II. 3. भोगेभ्यः—'the dat. by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "स्पृहेरीप्सितः' Pân. I. 4. 36. In the case of the root स्पृह् the object",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "desired is put in the dative case. स्पृहयालु—from स्पृह्+आलु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "by 'स्पृहिगृहि पतिदयिनिद्रातन्द्राश्रद्धाभ्य आलुच्—' Pân. III. 2.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "358; so गृहयालु, पतयालु &c. स्यूत—stitched; p. p. p. of सिव् 4 cl.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "भिक्षासक्तु—barley–flour (obtained by) begging. Cf. infra Mis.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "sl. 37.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 95. उपधानम्—pillow; fr. उप+धा+ल्युट् (अन). वितान—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "m. n. a canopy. वितन्यते इति fr. तन् with वि+घञ् (अ). विरतिवनिता–",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Cf. infra.mis. 39, कुरुत करुणामैत्रीप्रज्ञावधूजनसंगमम् where करुणा, मैत्री",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "and प्रज्ञा are likewise called wives. सुखम्—an adv. here. अतनु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "&c.—from the adj. तनु the fem. forms are तनु or तन्वी. भूति has",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "two meanings viz. (1) 'prosperity' as applicable to the king",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "and (2) 'ashes' as applicable to the Muni. Cf. Mis. Sl. 31. infra.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 96. स्वायत्त &c.—जितेन्द्रियः whose movements are under",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "control; who practises self-restraint. आस्यूत &c.—an एकदेशी",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "अन्वय. संप्रोत v. l. sewn together, patched with. शमसुखाभोग &c.—",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
